    <string name="settings_tools">Tools</string>
    <string name="setting_eraser_end">Preview the eraser end</string>
    <string name="setting_eraser_end_detail">The display draws the eraser end’s track at once while you erase, and Nib erases when you lift the pen. It works only while Instant ink is on. With the switch off, the page updates as you erase, which is slower.</string>
    <string name="settings_instant_ink">Instant ink (experimental)</string>
    <string name="setting_instant_ink">Instant ink</string>
    <string name="setting_instant_ink_detail">The display draws your pen strokes itself while you write, as Boox’s own apps do, so ink appears at once. It works only where the tablet’s firmware offers it, and it is still experimental. If strokes look wrong or leave marks, turn it off.</string>
    <string name="setting_instant_ink_on_note">Applies the next time you open a drawing.</string>
    <string name="setting_instant_ink_off_note">Nib draws every stroke itself, which is a little slower. The preview settings here and on the Display page have no effect while Instant ink is off. Applies the next time you open a drawing.</string>
    <string name="settings_pen">Pen</string>
    <string name="settings_fingers">Fingers</string>
    <string name="settings_panels">Panels</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_detail">Cards you drag stay where you leave them, separately in portrait and landscape.</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_reset">Restore every card beside its button</string>
    <string name="settings_panels_done">Every card is restored beside its button</string>
    <string name="settings_preview">Display preview</string>
    <string name="setting_marker_preview">Marker and highlighter preview</string>
    <string name="setting_marker_preview_detail">The display’s own preview can’t be see-through in most colours (measured on a Note Air6 C). Choose between a see-through grey and a solid colour.</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_grey">See-through grey</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_grey_detail">A see-through grey as light as your colour. What’s under the stroke stays visible, and your colour appears when you lift the pen.</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_solid">Solid colour</string>
    <string name="marker_preview_solid_detail">Your colour, roughly, covering what’s under the stroke until you lift the pen. On a Note Air6 C, blue shows as grey and very pale colours may not show.</string>
    <string name="settings_preview_detail">If the display’s preview looks wider or thinner than the stroke that replaces it, you can match the two. Tap the button below to open Match preview in Diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="setting_straight">Hold to draw a straight line</string>
    <string name="setting_straight_detail">Rest the pen at the end of a stroke for half a second and the stroke becomes a straight line from where it began. On the tablet, the display previews the stroke as drawn; the straight line replaces it when you lift.</string>
    <string name="setting_left_handed">Tools on the right</string>
    <string name="setting_left_handed_detail">Moves the pens, tools and sliders to the right edge. This suits drawing with the left hand.</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_drawing">Draw with a finger</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_drawing_detail">Lets a finger draw as well as the pen. When this is off, fingers only move the page and the pen is the only thing that draws.</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_pan">One finger moves the page</string>
    <string name="setting_finger_pan_detail">This works when fingers don’t draw. Two fingers always pinch to zoom, and move and turn the page.</string>
    <string name="setting_fast_gestures">Fast refresh while things move</string>
    <string name="setting_fast_gestures_detail">The display switches to its quick mode while fingers move, zoom or turn the page and while you drag a selection, as Boox’s own apps do. The screen is cleaned up once you stop. It works only while Instant ink is on.</string>
    <string name="setting_palm_guard">Palm guard</string>
    <string name="setting_palm_guard_detail">The display ignores finger touches on the canvas while the pen is near, so a resting hand can’t move the page. It works only while Instant ink is on. Not yet verified, so try it in Diagnostics › Lab first.</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal">Show the finished ink</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal_detail">While you write, the display draws its own quick preview of each stroke, and Nib’s finished ink replaces it. Choose when that happens.</string>
    <string name="reveal_auto">Auto</string>
    <string name="reveal_auto_detail">Chooses for you: “At breaks” for the pens the display previews faithfully, and “After a pause” for textured, blended and see-through ones.</string>
    <string name="reveal_breaks">At breaks</string>
    <string name="reveal_breaks_detail">The finished ink replaces the preview when you touch a control, open a panel, move the page or undo, as Boox Notes does. Quick writing stays quickest.</string>
    <string name="reveal_pause">After a pause</string>
    <string name="reveal_pause_detail">Once the pen rests, Nib puts its finished ink on the display without interrupting you. You set the length of the pause below.</string>
    <string name="reveal_every">After every stroke</string>
    <string name="reveal_every_detail">The finished ink replaces each stroke’s preview as soon as you lift the pen. This slows quick writing.</string>
    <string name="setting_reveal_pause">Pause before the finished ink</string>
    <string name="setting_gestures">Tap with two fingers to undo, with three to redo. Fingers are ignored while the pen is near the screen.</string>

