    <!-- Diagnostics › Lab -->
    <string name="diag_lab">Lab</string>
    <string name="diag_lab_help">Nib relies on some display commands that haven’t been seen working on a Note Air6 C yet. Try each one, then answer. Your answers go into Nib’s log.</string>
    <string name="lab_push_ink">Push ink</string>
    <string name="lab_push_controls">Push controls</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_end">Eraser end</string>
    <string name="lab_lasso">Lasso</string>
    <string name="lab_fast_mode">Fast mode</string>
    <string name="lab_palm_guard">Palm guard</string>
    <string name="lab_style_params">Style settings</string>
    <string name="lab_limit">Limit</string>
    <string name="lab_fed_stroke">Fed stroke</string>
    <string name="lab_pen_state_4">Pen state 4</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_painters">Eraser painters</string>
    <string name="lab_geometry">Geometry</string>
    <string name="lab_clean_screen">Clean screen</string>
    <string name="lab_push_ink_help">Draw a stroke in a band, then rest the pen for %1$s. Nib pushes its own finished ink to the display without letting a frame through. Did the preview become Nib’s exact stroke?</string>
    <string name="lab_push_controls_help">Draw several strokes without touching anything else. The counter is pushed to the display after each one while the display holds Nib’s frames. Did it keep up?</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_end_help">Draw a few strokes, then turn the pen round and rub them out with the eraser end. Nib asks the display to draw the eraser’s track. Nib erases the strokes when you lift the pen.</string>
    <string name="lab_lasso_help">Draw a loop in the lasso band. Nib asks the display to draw the path as a dashed line, which disappears when you lift the pen.</string>
    <string name="lab_fast_mode_help">Fast mode is the display’s quick refresh while things move. Draw something, then drag the drawing area with a finger, once with fast mode on and once with it off. The grid and your strokes move with your finger.</string>
    <string name="lab_palm_guard_help">Turn Palm guard on, hold the pen just above the drawing area and rest your hand on it. While the pen is near, finger touches there should do nothing. If fingers still do nothing a second after you take the pen away, answer Stuck off.</string>
    <string name="lab_style_params_help">The sliders set the display’s own fountain pen style, and Nib sends each change as you make it. Draw after each change: does the preview’s response to pressure change? Nib puts the display’s own values back when you leave.</string>
    <string name="lab_limit_help">Nib asks the display to preview only inside the middle band, and gives it that band’s place on the screen. Draw across all three bands.</string>
    <string name="lab_fed_stroke_help">Nib pauses the preview and feeds a line of points across the middle of the drawing area to the display. Nib asks the display for the stroke width at each point. Watch the drawing area as you tap Feed a test stroke.</string>
    <string name="lab_pen_state_4_help">Once this page is open, Nib asks the display to hold pen state 4, which Boox’s pen software calls erasing but never uses. Draw with the pen tip: does the display preview anything? Nib records in the log which state the display reports back.</string>
    <string name="lab_eraser_painters_help">The display has nine ways to draw the eraser’s track, called painters. Each band tries a different one, from 0 at the top to 8 at the bottom. Rub with the eraser end in every band and answer for each band whether its track showed.</string>
    <string name="lab_geometry_help">What the display reports about its own size and how it maps onto the screen, for the way the tablet is turned now. Turn the tablet, then tap Read again.</string>
    <string name="lab_clean_screen_help">These are the two ways Boox’s reader app cleans a colour screen. Tap each one, then answer how the screen looked.</string>
